# Marker Size and Color on Bubble Charts

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

Combine `marker.size` and `marker.color` as lists with a `colorscale` to encode two dimensions.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: [1, 2, 3, 4],
    y: [10, 11, 12, 13],
    mode: "markers",
    marker: %{
      color: [120, 125, 130, 135],
      size: [40, 60, 80, 100],
      colorscale: "Viridis",
      showscale: true
    }
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Marker Size and Color on Bubble Charts")
|> Plotly.show()
```
